^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-07-26 23:17] observe — Initialized plan for geometric analysis tooling across spw-seed, spw-lsp, and spw-cli.
 >>[2026-07-26 23:40] observe — Ran spw geometry on a stdin fixture; report self-contradicts. Sigils inside a quoted string counted as operators, and a `{` inside that string produced a false unbalanced-brace lesson while the AST-derived brace counts stayed correct.
 >>[2026-07-26 23:40] decide — Reframed scope around the census defect. Lexer fixity stays upstream (it supplies site/arity), but the spine is now: AST census -> order -> shape -> baseline.
 >>[2026-07-26 23:40] taste — Previous revision listed four paths that do not exist (matchers/operator.ts, matchers/container.ts, handlers/hover.ts, handlers/diagnostics.ts, ls/index.ts) and omitted geometry-inspect.ts, the module holding the defect. Corrected.
 >>[2026-07-26 23:40] taste — geometry-inspect.ts at 184 lines cannot absorb census + rhythm + shape + lessons under the 400-line target; split into four single-concern modules. form-geometry.ts (1209) and form-ladders.ts (943) are already over guard — import, never extend.
 >>[2026-07-26 23:40] observe — vitest.seed.config.ts includes both src/seed/**/*.test.ts and packages/spw-seed/src/**/*.test.ts, so package-local seed tests do run.
 >>[2026-07-26 23:55] observe — ONF is already the substrate the shape work needs: ONFNode is {sigil, args[], frames}, positional and label-free, and '_' is already the hole sigil. Anti-unified templates are therefore ONF terms, not a new datatype.
 >>[2026-07-26 23:55] observe — The shape primitive is declared but unimplemented. onf.ts states 'momentum frames are excluded from semantic hash' as an invariant; garden names 'ONF shape hash' as a formula kind; grep for semanticHash|shapeHash|structuralHash returns zero hits. Commit 6 redeems a promise rather than adding an idea.
 >>[2026-07-26 23:55] decide — Dropped capsule/couple disambiguation from scope. types/coupling.ts already discriminates CouplingForm operator|boundary over the six-way PairedBoundaryKind registry, and normalize.ts stamps it. The bare `<` container token from the lexer is correct; disambiguation is downstream and already done.
 >>[2026-07-26 23:55] decide — Narrowed commit 2 from 'add fixity metadata' to 'populate what onf.ts already declares'. normalize.ts stamps actPlacement in several sites already; the gap is parser position, which onf.ts flags as 'often unset'.
 >>[2026-07-26 23:58] decide — Named the primitive shapeFingerprint over shapeHash, at the user's prompting. hashString is content identity across mutation-automata, range-transform, and form-geometry; collision there is failure, here it is the finding. Added commit 5 as a vocab pass so the reconciliation lands before the implementation.
 >>[2026-07-27 13:10] observe — plan-ecology sweep: .spw/patterns/surface-identity.spw now holds the shared identity vocabulary. shape_fingerprint is declared there; commit 5 settles the name against that surface rather than against this plan alone.
 >>[2026-09-30 16:54] revise — stay dormant. Operator physics is a scrutiny instrument, not a CLI product. The ops=3 repro (quoted sigils counted, false unbalanced brace) blocks any fingerprint or editor geometry that would teach the wrong charge.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:29] verify — re-ran the stdin repro through spw geometry: still prints ops=3 (! ^ ~) and the lesson 'Unbalanced open braces (balance=1)' while braces=2 from the AST path; censusOperators in geometry-inspect.ts still scans characters. The defect stands.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:29] revise — reconciled commits with git: ~[1] landed; ~[2] and ~[4] to ~[9] deferred behind the 2026-09-30 dormancy; ~[10] merged into ~[3] so the one live commit fixes the defect and pins the repro. Closed hygiene: the LSP and neovim drift is gone from the working tree (git status shows only plan files and .gitignore). Noted that FormFingerprint (spw.fingerprint/1, 5f181249) already owns the word fingerprint as a node-count signature; no semanticHash, shapeHash or shapeFingerprint exists in packages/.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:31] revise — convention: resolved questions and landed commits are kept in ^["done"] (resolved(label) and shipped) rather than deleted; ^["commits"] keeps a pointer comment.
 >>[2026-10-12 15:37] revise — Commits named per the convention in 90c58bbc: 2 landed, 8 planned, 1 dropped.
}

^["open"]{
 ?[fallback]: "Do prose-heavy .spw surfaces parse well enough that an AST census does not go blind where the char scan was merely noisy? Decides whether fallback:true is a rare path or the common one."
 ?[fixity_yield]: "What fraction of operator nodes can recover fixity from parser position? onf.ts says 'often unset'. If low, an arity-keyed census loses resolution and ~[ast_operator_census] should key on sigil x site only; this decides whether the deferred ~[parser_fixity_stamps] is worth reheating."
 ?[recurrence]: "What min-recur threshold separates idiom from accident for shape fingerprints? Needs corpus data from the deferred ~[onf_shape_fingerprint]; do not hand-pick it earlier."
}

^["resolved"]{
 $[vocab]: "Resolved 2026-07-26. Three names existed for one idea: onf.ts 'semantic hash' (declared invariant, never implemented), garden plan 'ONF shape hash' (~#kinds.structural), and this plan's 'fingerprint'. Settled on shapeFingerprint, keeping the ONF-shape qualifier. Rationale: hashString already means content identity here (inputHash/outputHash, beforeHash/afterHash, range-transform source id) where collision is failure; a shape fingerprint is many-to-one by design, where collision is the finding. Inverted collision semantics should not share a head noun. settle_shape_fingerprint does the reconciliation before onf_shape_fingerprint implements."
}

